## 18. Mandatory Media Processing, CAS Deduplication & Zero Disk Space Leak Engine (Strict Rule)
- Mandatory Centralized Gateway: Direct file storage via raw Laravel methods (`$request->file('...')->store('...')`, `Storage::putFile(...)`) is strictly prohibited. All media uploads (images, PDFs, documents, avatars) MUST pass through `app(MediaOptimizationService::class)` (`optimizeImage()`, `optimizePdf()`, or `optimize()`).
- Compulsory WebP & Compression: All uploaded images must be converted to WebP format at 80% quality, width downscaled capped at 1920px (`scaleDown(width: 1920)`), and all EXIF metadata stripped. Upscaling is prohibited.
- PDF Optimization: Process PDFs via Ghostscript (`gs`) using `/ebook` profile (150dpi, compatibility 1.4) with resilient fallback.
- Content-Addressable Storage (CAS) Deduplication: Store files using cryptographic SHA-256 content hashes (`{sha256}.webp` / `{sha256}.pdf`). If identical content is uploaded by any user, reuse the existing file on disk with zero duplicate bytes written.
- Mandatory Reference-Aware Safe Deletion: Unconditional deletion via `Storage::delete($path)` is strictly prohibited for shared media. Always check references via `MediaOptimizationService::isAssetInUse($path)` or call `MediaOptimizationService::safeDelete($path, $disk, $excludeEntityId)`. Physical assets are preserved as long as references exist (> 0) and only unlinked when active references reach zero.
- Process & Destroy Protocol: Intermediate temp files in `storage/app/temp-media` or system temp must be immediately purged via `@unlink()` (`destroyTempFiles()`). Zero temp or raw files may linger on the server disk.

